{"rawTokenId is never null-checked - line 73 re-validates grantType (which was already checked on line 72) but never validates rawTokenId. If rawTokenId is null, the field is silently stored as null, getRawTokenId() returns null, and encodeTokenId concatenates it as the literal string \"...prefix:null\" \u2014 generating a corrupted token ID": 0.9584235548973083, "Duplicate-shortcut validation only catches mismatched map sizes \u2014 not the duplicate itself. When two grant-type factories share the same shortcut, one entry silently overwrites the other in grantsByShortcuts, leaving decoding broken for the overwritten grant. The check would catch the size difference, but the thrown message names the overwritten entry \u2014 making debugging harder": 0.652550458908081, "Non-atomic lazy update of two ConcurrentHashMaps can produce a briefly inconsistent state. Between the grantsByShortcuts.put(shortcut, grantType) and grantsToShortcuts.put(grantType, shortcut) calls, a concurrent reader may find an entry in grantsByShortcuts before grantsToShortcuts has been updated": 0.6661266088485718}